WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.050
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.320 --> 00:07.070
Oh la la! Takashi, you dated Rui?

3
00:07.070 --> 00:08.871
Yeah, that's right.

4
00:08.871 --> 00:11.358
That was four years ago.

5
00:11.358 --> 00:12.887
Was it really that long ago?

6
00:12.887 --> 00:13.888
Yeah.

7
00:15.194 --> 00:17.549
Wait, I honestly can't imagine it.

8
00:19.735 --> 00:20.735
Actually, I can.

9
00:22.465 --> 00:24.232
Come on. Take a seat.

10
00:25.628 --> 00:27.624
Oh, it's beautiful.

11
00:27.624 --> 00:31.199
Wow, this looks so tasty.

12
00:31.199 --> 00:33.784
There's mango too. Miyata's favorite.

13
00:33.784 --> 00:35.118
I'll have some later.

14
00:37.174 --> 00:38.290
Senpai.

15
00:38.290 --> 00:39.118
Hm?

16
00:39.957 --> 00:41.416
Oh.

17
00:41.416 --> 00:43.546
Wait. "Senpai"?

18
00:44.378 --> 00:45.959
Aren't you dating?

19
00:45.959 --> 00:50.133
He was my junior in high school.

20
00:50.133 --> 00:54.215
And he still calls you "Senpai"?

21
00:56.368 --> 00:57.689
You really...

22
00:59.184 --> 01:00.184
are pure.

23
01:02.751 --> 01:04.731
Are you teasing me?

24
01:05.588 --> 01:08.568
Not at all. I didn't mean it that way.

25
01:23.417 --> 01:25.175
Well then...

26
01:25.175 --> 01:26.852
Santé!

27
01:26.852 --> 01:29.573
Santé!

28
01:35.137 --> 01:36.219
Mm.

29
01:36.219 --> 01:37.471
How is it?

30
01:37.471 --> 01:39.099
- Delicious. - It's delicious.

31
01:39.099 --> 01:40.099
So good!

32
01:40.996 --> 01:43.979
So, Kyosuke, where did you meet Rui?

33
01:44.688 --> 01:47.883
He designed the label on this wine bottle.

34
01:47.883 --> 01:49.746
He's a rising young designer,

35
01:49.746 --> 01:53.213
and since he's so wonderful, I just had to hire him.

36
01:53.213 --> 01:55.427
A designer?

37
01:55.427 --> 01:57.232
Wait, is Rui...

38
01:57.232 --> 01:58.911
Rui Taniguchi?

39
01:58.911 --> 02:03.483
The youngest ever to win the Japan Designers Association Award?

40
02:03.483 --> 02:04.483
Huh?

41
02:06.176 --> 02:08.575
I'm so happy!

42
02:09.585 --> 02:13.395
Miyata, you knew about me?

43
02:14.218 --> 02:16.540
I'm in the publishing industry, so...

44
02:16.540 --> 02:18.471
Let's dig in!

45
02:21.016 --> 02:22.267
I want the white fish.

46
02:22.267 --> 02:24.147
All of Senpai's exes...

47
02:25.187 --> 02:29.137
are people making waves in their own fields.

48
02:32.389 --> 02:35.962
First-rate people attract first-rate people, huh?

49
03:38.218 --> 03:40.692
So, are you two still just coworkers?

50
03:42.406 --> 03:43.461
Us?

51
03:44.182 --> 03:46.184
Who knows?

52
03:46.977 --> 03:47.978
Beats me.

53
03:51.203 --> 03:52.482
What about that guy before?

54
03:55.177 --> 03:59.102
Oh, we just went on a date, that's all.

55
04:01.065 --> 04:02.576
Did that bother you?

56
04:07.324 --> 04:09.242
Oh, not at all.

57
04:12.628 --> 04:15.341
So? How are you two doing?

58
04:15.341 --> 04:16.757
Are things going well?

59
04:19.243 --> 04:21.422
I'm so happy it's a waste to sleep.

60
04:24.189 --> 04:27.434
I'm grateful I was lucky enough to meet him again.

61
04:28.430 --> 04:31.746
These two work together too.

62
04:31.746 --> 04:33.882
They're even putting out a book.

63
04:33.882 --> 04:34.882
What?

64
04:35.903 --> 04:37.235
I want to do the design!

65
04:39.635 --> 04:41.823
Well, I don't know about that...

66
04:44.113 --> 04:46.035
- Please do! - Huh?

67
04:46.780 --> 04:50.207
It'd be an honor to work with you.

68
04:52.034 --> 04:54.824
Yes!

69
04:57.206 --> 04:59.257
No matter what, okay?

70
05:04.094 --> 05:05.094
Yes.

71
05:05.894 --> 05:07.974
An editor never goes back on his word.

72
05:10.413 --> 05:12.420
Merci!

73
05:17.276 --> 05:20.445
Sugimoto, a toast!

74
05:20.445 --> 05:21.489
Shall we go up?

75
05:25.668 --> 05:26.668
Au revoir!

76
05:27.730 --> 05:30.372
Goodbye! See you!

77
05:47.170 --> 05:48.431
Why would you do that?

78
05:51.969 --> 05:56.008
If a popular designer is asking to do it,

79
05:56.008 --> 05:58.066
a proper editor can't say no.

80
06:29.891 --> 06:32.100
Want me to help you out of your kimono?

81
06:33.657 --> 06:34.853
Yes, please.

82
06:39.541 --> 06:44.571
I want to act genuine too and just call him Takashi.

83
07:09.949 --> 07:10.949
Morning.

84
07:11.677 --> 07:12.677
Good morning.

85
07:18.500 --> 07:20.711
Maybe I'll buy some on the way home today.

86
07:24.145 --> 07:27.727
Don't go buying expensive imported stuff again.

87
07:28.942 --> 07:31.701
The regular kind is fine. The regular kind.

88
07:50.982 --> 07:52.138
Takashi...

89
07:54.766 --> 07:58.974
I want to center it on Iwanaga's charming way of speaking,

90
07:58.974 --> 08:02.674
and make it a business book that reaches younger readers too.

91
08:02.674 --> 08:05.253
- For the cover... - What will his photo be like?

92
08:05.253 --> 08:06.416
Well...

93
08:08.161 --> 08:09.161
Like this?

94
08:11.171 --> 08:12.908
- Arms crossed? - Yes.

95
08:12.908 --> 08:14.041
And?

96
08:14.041 --> 08:18.145
Or maybe something like this.

97
08:18.145 --> 08:19.527
And?

98
08:19.527 --> 08:20.667
Like this.

99
08:20.667 --> 08:23.156
- Yeah, that's lame. - Huh?

100
08:23.156 --> 08:28.049
I want visuals that look like they belong in a fashion magazine.

101
08:29.760 --> 08:32.596
You don't usually see that in business books.

102
08:32.596 --> 08:34.415
Shouldn't the cover attract buyers?

103
08:36.037 --> 08:37.037
I see.

104
08:37.672 --> 08:42.051
Hmm, I want a photo shoot with a lot of scenarios.

105
08:45.317 --> 08:49.030
What kind of scenarios do you like, Miyata?

106
08:50.798 --> 08:51.798
Me?

107
08:52.984 --> 08:54.826
Just personal curiosity.

108
08:56.902 --> 08:59.490
Is he prying into my relationship with Senpai?

109
09:01.917 --> 09:05.222
My preferences don't matter anyway.

110
09:05.222 --> 09:08.423
I see. Then I'll prepare some options on my end.

111
09:15.288 --> 09:16.806
Nice.

112
09:17.821 --> 09:19.267
Beautiful.

113
09:25.107 --> 09:27.275
Do we have flowers?

114
09:27.275 --> 09:28.860
Please bring the flowers!

115
09:36.285 --> 09:37.876
His skin is so nice.

116
09:37.876 --> 09:39.427
Of course it is.

117
09:39.427 --> 09:41.886
Takashi takes good care of his skin.

118
09:41.886 --> 09:43.174
- Thanks. - Yeah!

119
09:43.174 --> 09:44.720
Your outfit's cool too.

120
09:44.720 --> 09:47.017
But isn't this a bit too flashy?

121
09:47.017 --> 09:48.041
- Professor. - What?

122
09:48.041 --> 09:52.580
You're super cool. It suits you perfectly.

123
09:52.580 --> 09:53.573
Thanks Rui.

124
09:53.573 --> 09:55.810
- Not at all. - Um, it's almost time.

125
09:55.810 --> 09:56.668
Oh, okay.

126
09:56.668 --> 09:57.902
Oh, wait a moment.

127
09:58.560 --> 10:02.340
Let's give this spot a bit more volume.

128
10:03.265 --> 10:05.301
And here too, like this...

129
10:05.939 --> 10:07.781
Yeah, you look amazing.

130
10:07.781 --> 10:08.781
Nice work, Rui.

131
10:16.828 --> 10:18.701
What do you think, Miyata?

132
10:21.638 --> 10:22.789
I think it's good.

133
10:24.615 --> 10:27.210
Don't you have anything more to say?

134
10:29.799 --> 10:30.799
Um...

135
10:32.816 --> 10:34.134
I think it's really good.

136
10:38.129 --> 10:39.293
Oh, well.

137
10:40.162 --> 10:42.883
We're done here then.

138
10:42.883 --> 10:46.155
All right! We're done.

139
10:46.155 --> 10:48.340
- You look amazing. - Thank you.

140
11:07.835 --> 11:09.993
Takashi, you look amazing!

141
11:09.993 --> 11:12.033
Wow, nice. Super cool.

142
11:12.033 --> 11:14.924
So fashionable. So handsome.

143
11:14.924 --> 11:16.009
Not bad, huh?

144
11:16.009 --> 11:17.553
How about this?

145
11:17.553 --> 11:20.371
He's great at pumping people up.

146
11:20.371 --> 11:22.683
When Rui gives compliments like that,

147
11:22.683 --> 11:26.645
even Iwanaga naturally gets excited.

148
11:26.645 --> 11:29.603
Would he really be that simple-minded?

149
11:29.603 --> 11:31.207
Huh?

150
11:31.207 --> 11:34.110
Oh, no, it's nothing.

151
11:37.155 --> 11:39.176
Put your hand a bit near your mouth.

152
11:39.176 --> 11:41.242
Yes, yes, and angle it.

153
11:43.095 --> 11:46.289
Work. It's just work.

154
11:47.309 --> 11:48.816
Okay! Let's go!

155
11:56.144 --> 11:58.528
- Here? - Yeah, great.

156
11:58.528 --> 11:59.528
Rest your elbow.

157
12:01.887 --> 12:02.887
And your hands.

158
12:03.849 --> 12:05.052
Good.

159
12:05.052 --> 12:08.874
Work. It's just wo...

160
12:08.874 --> 12:11.620
Raise your right hand a bit.

161
12:11.620 --> 12:12.816
Is this right?

162
12:12.816 --> 12:16.004
Wait, is this really just work?

163
12:18.071 --> 12:19.282
Sugimoto?

164
12:19.282 --> 12:21.089
Rui invited me.

165
12:21.089 --> 12:23.228
I came because I was worried about you.

166
12:23.228 --> 12:23.911
Amazing.

167
12:23.911 --> 12:25.455
Why would you worry about me?

168
12:27.167 --> 12:30.458
Oh my, aren't those two way too close?

169
12:31.808 --> 12:34.379
I don't really care.

170
12:36.924 --> 12:41.156
Man, I can't believe Rui was Takashi's ex.

171
12:41.156 --> 12:43.222
When it comes to Rui,

172
12:43.222 --> 12:47.563
he's totally different from you and his ex from college, so I was shocked.

173
12:49.745 --> 12:51.271
His college ex?

174
12:55.150 --> 12:57.598
I hear he's the only guy who ever dumped Takashi.

175
12:59.517 --> 13:01.906
Well, excluding you from high school.

176
13:09.164 --> 13:12.480
Takashi really does suit flowers.

177
13:12.480 --> 13:14.461
- He does. - They suit him perfectly.

178
13:20.977 --> 13:21.977
How was it?

179
13:22.874 --> 13:26.585
Oh, I thought it was really good.

180
13:27.407 --> 13:28.891
Thanks to you.

181
13:29.879 --> 13:32.962
There's no feeling in that at all.

182
13:34.427 --> 13:35.427
Oh.

183
13:36.973 --> 13:40.641
If you don't like it, Miyata, then all my hard work was for nothing.

184
13:41.945 --> 13:44.979
Well, we'll talk more at the next meeting.

185
13:46.312 --> 13:47.312
Good work.

186
13:48.756 --> 13:49.856
Sugimoto!

187
13:54.750 --> 13:55.750
Good work.

188
13:57.603 --> 13:58.603
What now?

189
13:59.715 --> 14:02.426
I'm heading back to the office for now.

190
14:02.426 --> 14:04.742
Hmm, I see.

191
14:05.883 --> 14:08.765
So don't worry about me. Just go home, Senpai.

192
14:13.313 --> 14:14.313
Senpai?

193
14:15.866 --> 14:19.067
And here I thought we'd finally get some time alone.

194
14:20.880 --> 14:22.612
We'll see each other again soon.

195
14:24.725 --> 14:26.532
Then I'll head off first.

196
14:34.916 --> 14:37.768
There's a good Malaysian place.

197
14:37.768 --> 14:39.366
Or, well, there's Thai too.

198
14:40.797 --> 14:42.131
Tom yum kung.

199
14:42.131 --> 14:43.010
Hm?

200
14:43.010 --> 14:44.075
Vietnamese is fine too.

201
14:46.637 --> 14:49.700
Senpai, how many lovers have you had?

202
14:49.700 --> 14:51.224
That's a secret.

203
14:53.146 --> 14:56.086
He's not good enough for you.

204
14:58.918 --> 15:01.109
Aren't those two way too close?

205
15:03.320 --> 15:06.328
Who gave you that watch?

206
15:06.328 --> 15:08.617
Someone I was close with in college.

207
15:08.617 --> 15:11.431
I hear he's the only guy who ever dumped Takashi.

208
15:35.868 --> 15:36.868
Welcome back.

209
15:40.148 --> 15:42.974
When he sees his exes,

210
15:42.974 --> 15:45.319
he smiles like that to them too.

211
15:47.908 --> 15:48.908
What's wrong?

212
16:09.449 --> 16:12.221
All of this is your fault, Senpai.

213
16:24.573 --> 16:27.528
Just stay like this for a little while, please.

214
16:33.011 --> 16:34.011
Okay.

215
16:47.258 --> 16:50.385
I'm the most important person to you, right?

216
16:54.973 --> 16:57.779
Don't you know...

217
17:03.972 --> 17:05.316
how crazy I am about you?

218
19:10.430 --> 19:14.111
This one, this one, and this one. What do you think?

219
19:15.162 --> 19:16.196
I think they're good.

220
19:17.116 --> 19:19.158
Did you actually give it some thought?

221
19:20.702 --> 19:25.385
Well, you know Senpai's charm much better than I do,

222
19:25.385 --> 19:26.916
so my opinion isn't important.

223
19:28.168 --> 19:30.002
What's gotten into you?

224
19:31.896 --> 19:34.423
I can't bring out that expression in him.

225
19:35.979 --> 19:37.093
Are you okay?

226
19:39.800 --> 19:42.056
I might not be.

227
19:49.874 --> 19:50.874
Miyata,

228
19:52.074 --> 19:55.235
do you know why I broke up with Takashi?

229
19:56.697 --> 19:58.447
Huh? No.

230
20:00.374 --> 20:02.314
When I was dating Takashi,

231
20:03.122 --> 20:05.579
I ended up just like you are now, Miyata.

232
20:07.788 --> 20:09.740
Where were you yesterday?

233
20:09.740 --> 20:12.546
I went to eat Uzbek food with friends.

234
20:12.546 --> 20:16.773
Friends? Who? A guy? Your ex?

235
20:18.744 --> 20:20.678
I got too absorbed in Takashi...

236
20:22.628 --> 20:25.391
and couldn't focus on work anymore.

237
20:29.188 --> 20:33.612
So I'm the one who said it.

238
20:33.612 --> 20:35.342
That we should break up.

239
20:38.780 --> 20:43.724
Miyata, every time you look at Takashi now,

240
20:43.724 --> 20:50.458
have you ever thought, "Oh, I bet he's made that face to his exes too."

241
20:53.921 --> 20:58.705
That's what they call retroactive jealousy.

242
20:59.843 --> 21:02.683
"Retroactive jealousy"?

243
21:02.683 --> 21:05.140
Every time your lover does something,

244
21:05.140 --> 21:08.799
you can't help thinking he did the same with his past lovers.

245
21:09.753 --> 21:12.380
The most unproductive emotion in human history.

246
21:14.864 --> 21:20.429
I know it's ridiculous. I think so too.

247
21:22.498 --> 21:27.787
But I do like how devoted you are, Miyata.

248
21:30.643 --> 21:32.291
I think it's really wonderful.

249
21:36.018 --> 21:41.676
So I don't want you to feel jealous or anything like that toward me.

250
21:50.067 --> 21:52.409
Because the reason I took this job

251
21:52.409 --> 21:54.916
was that I wanted to see you again, Miyata.

252
21:56.236 --> 21:57.236
Huh?

253
21:58.151 --> 22:01.424
So relax and let's work together, okay?

254
22:03.109 --> 22:05.302
Now I feel even more tense.

255
22:07.650 --> 22:11.239
Rui Taniguchi. What a terrifying guy!

256
22:14.126 --> 22:15.991
Then shall we proceed?

257
22:15.991 --> 22:16.991
Yeah.

258
22:17.879 --> 22:20.559
Better than having his arrow pointed at Senpai, I guess.

259
22:22.115 --> 22:23.301
How about this one?

260
22:24.303 --> 22:25.940
Miyata, that's super cool.

261
22:25.940 --> 22:27.681
- It's awesome. - Right?

262
22:27.681 --> 22:30.498
So good. Any others?

263
22:31.935 --> 22:33.360
Welcome back.

264
22:33.360 --> 22:34.360
I'm home.

265
22:35.355 --> 22:36.841
Did you stop by somewhere?

266
22:36.841 --> 22:38.894
Yeah, the real estate agency.

267
22:38.894 --> 22:40.485
Do you have a moment?

268
22:40.485 --> 22:41.488
Yes.

269
22:43.487 --> 22:46.590
You mentioned before that you'd like to live here.

270
22:46.590 --> 22:48.671
Oh, that luxury place?

271
22:48.671 --> 22:49.671
Yeah.

272
22:57.063 --> 22:59.294
I signed the contract today.

273
23:02.645 --> 23:06.327
I wanted a place where we could spend forever together.

274
23:17.077 --> 23:18.605
We can move in next week.

275
23:35.230 --> 23:36.230
Miyata?

276
23:50.472 --> 23:52.551
I want you to feel the weight of my love.

277
23:52.551 --> 23:54.838
You might change your mind, right?

278
23:54.838 --> 23:56.562
I take that back.

279
23:56.562 --> 23:59.436
Can we really be happy together?
